#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fourier_cos_coefficient

#% text
# `fourier_cos_coefficient(f, t, n)` gives the `n`-th coefficient of the Fourier cosine series of `f`, `2/pi` times the integral of `f cos(n t)` for `t` from 0 to `pi`: the cosine coefficient of the even extension of `f` from `[0, pi]`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# With `fourier_parameters: [a, b]` the coefficient is `2 abs(b)/pi` times the integral of `f cos(b n t)` over `[0, pi/abs(b)]`.

#% item
# A symbolic `n` is taken to be a positive integer: the result is the generic coefficient, with the exceptional positive indices as cases of a `piecewise` (or a `discrete_delta`).

#% item
# Lists of variables and indices give the coefficients of the products of cosines.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fourier_cos_coefficient(t^2, t, n)
#% output
#= 4*(-1)^n/n^2

#% cell
fourier_cos_coefficient(abs(t), t, 3)
#% output
#= -4/(9*pi)

#% cell
fourier_cos_coefficient(x^2*y, [x, y], [3, 5])
#% output
#= 16/(225*pi)

#% cell
fourier_cos_coefficient(cos(2*t), t, n)
#% output
#= discrete_delta(-2 + n)

#% section
# See also

#% text
